      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "SHADES OF MIKI (12) is hard to knock after winning here last start in NR up to 75 grade, scoring by a head despite racing wide early and rating 1:54.8. The second-row gate make it less straightforward, but his Albion Park 2138m record is a strength. DONNIE MAC (11) comes through a similar prizemoney race after beating Messerati at Riverina Paceway over 2270m as a well-supported favourite, and his prior Riverina run was in another NR up to 70 at a solid mile rate, so the form is sound if he handles his first local look. SWEET DREAMS NZ (2) was competitive when fourth at Redcliffe and has the Amanda Turnbull association in her favour, though she was safely held two back in NR up to 80 company and has a distance query. ANGUS FINN NZ (8) brings genuine Newcastle form, including a close third in NR up to 63 company and a prior run in a fast NR up to 90, but the second-row draw and first Queensland run temper the confidence.",
